{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1574873342,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1Mjk0NjUxOTg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3896","origin":"github"},"title":"Consolidate commit message specification","message":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3316 is asking for `-m/--message` for all commiting commands. There are quite a few, hence this would be a project of some size. https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/3883 already started, and https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/3893 suggests to add special meaning to a `-m` without an option. There is also: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3882\n\nIt would be good to thing to think this through a bit more and then make one consolidated effort (or at least a plan for such).\n\n**Keep it minimal**: we have plenty of command that need message opts, but `save` as two (`-m` and `-F`). I propose to kill `-F` and replace it with a `file:` argument prefix detection than is then accessible to all commands\n\n**Centralize**: Message file handling should move out of `save` and be extended to a  common helper that deal with any message handling. I think it is worth pondering whether we want a class/function that can be used internally to signal and handle interactive message input, like approached in #3893, possibly with templating for subdatasets as done in https://github.com/datalad/datalad-revolution/pull/71. But there is another templating aspect too: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2100\n\n**What about tagging?**: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3371","files":null}]}